IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 76(10) to (15) -- the route by special resolution, the written-means timing rule, the Court's declaration,
-- who may oppose in Court and the Court's powers and bars, the lodging of the Court's order, and the saving for directors' duties.
-- Layer 1. Each paragraph of subsection (10) is its own function; the route function takes their answers.
--
-- HOW THE ROUTE ANSWERS. As for ss (9A) to (9BA): the route is a carve-out named for a permission, so JUST TRUE when every paragraph holds and NOTHING otherwise (marker {F-A7}).
-- Paragraphs (b), (d) and (g) speak only of a case "where" the company is the subsidiary of a listed corporation, or of an ultimate holding company in Singapore:
-- where that case is absent the paragraph imposes nothing, so the function answers NOTHING (limited by its own wording) and the route reads NOTHING there as "nothing required" (fork F-A13).
-- The rendering repeats a paragraph label where a paragraph runs on after its sub-paragraphs: (b) at lines 7838-7840, (c) at 7858-7869 and (h) at 7936-7937 (NOTES.md, finding).

§ `Section 76(10): the route by special resolution`

-- (10)(a): the company, by special resolution, resolves to give financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, that acquisition.
-- src:7816 | (10) Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company of
-- src:7817 | financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, an
-- src:7818 | acquisition or proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units of
-- src:7819 | shares in the company or in a holding company or ultimate holding
-- src:7820 | company (as the case may be) of the company if —
-- src:7822 | (a) the company, by special resolution, resolves to give
-- src:7823 | financial assistance for the purpose of or in connection
-- src:7824 | with, that acquisition;
@ref s 76(10)(a) (src:7816-7824)
GIVEN `the company has resolved by special resolution to give financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(a) the company has resolved by special resolution to give the assistance` MEANS
    IF `the company has resolved by special resolution to give financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, the acquisition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the company, by special resolution, resolves to give financial assistance for the purpose of or in connection with, that acquisition" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(b): where (i) the company is a subsidiary of a listed corporation; or (ii) the company is not a subsidiary of a listed corporation but is a subsidiary whose ultimate holding company is
-- incorporated in Singapore, ... . This function says whether paragraph (b) applies. "Listed" is s 4(1) (keel), "subsidiary" is s 5(1) and "ultimate holding company" is s 5A (keel).
-- src:7826 | (b) where —
-- src:7828 | (i) the company is a subsidiary of a listed corporation;
-- src:7829 | or
-- src:7834 | (ii) the company is not a subsidiary of a listed
-- src:7835 | corporation but is a subsidiary whose ultimate
-- src:7836 | holding company is incorporated in Singapore,
@ref s 76(10)(b) (src:7826-7836)
GIVEN `the other corporation controls the composition of the board of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firstmentioned corporation is a subsidiary of a corporation which is the other corporation's subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or corporation has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or corporation has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firstmentioned corporation is itself a subsidiary of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ultimate holding company of the company is incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(b) paragraph (b) applies to the company` MEANS
    IF     (    (`s 5(1) the corporation is deemed to be a subsidiary of the other corporation` `the other corporation controls the composition of the board of the firstmentioned corporation` `the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power of the firstmentioned corporation` `the firstmentioned corporation is a subsidiary of a corporation which is the other corporation's subsidiary` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            AND (`s 4(1) "listed" the company or corporation is listed` `the company or corporation has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` `the company or corporation has been removed from that official list` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
       OR (    (`s 5A the firstmentioned corporation is the ultimate holding company of the other corporation` `the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned corporation` `the firstmentioned corporation is itself a subsidiary of a corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND `the ultimate holding company of the company is incorporated in Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where (i) the company is a subsidiary of a listed corporation; or (ii) the company is not a subsidiary of a listed corporation but is a subsidiary whose ultimate holding company is incorporated in Singapore" -- a "where" gate that fails: periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the paragraph then asks nothing of the parent (fork F-A13)

-- (10)(b), the approval: the listed corporation or the ultimate holding company (as the case may be) has, by special resolution, approved the giving of the financial assistance.
-- src:7838 | (b) the listed corporation or the ultimate holding company (as
-- src:7839 | the case may be) has, by special resolution, approved the
-- src:7840 | giving of the financial assistance;
@ref s 76(10)(b) (src:7838-7840)
GIVEN `paragraph (b) applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the listed corporation or the ultimate holding company has, by special resolution, approved the giving of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(b) the listed corporation or ultimate holding company has approved the giving by special resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `paragraph (b) applies to the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company mentioned in (b)(i) or (ii), which exists only where (b) applies
    ELSE (IF `the listed corporation or the ultimate holding company has, by special resolution, approved the giving of the financial assistance`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) ... the listed corporation or the ultimate holding company (as the case may be) has, by special resolution, approved the giving of the financial assistance" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(c): the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution in (a) as a special resolution sets out (i) particulars of the assistance proposed and the reasons for the proposal;
-- (ii) the effect on the financial position of the company and, where the company is in a group, of the group; and is accompanied by a copy of a statement made in accordance with a resolution of
-- the directors, setting out the names of any directors who voted against the resolution and the reasons why, signed by not less than 2 directors, stating whether, in the opinion of the directors who
-- voted in favour, after taking into account the financial position of the company (including future and contingent liabilities), the giving would be likely to prejudice materially the interests of
-- the creditors or members of the company or any class of them.
-- src:7842 | (c) the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution
-- src:7843 | referred to in paragraph (a) as a special resolution sets
-- src:7844 | out —
-- src:7846 | (i) particulars of the financial assistance proposed to be
-- src:7847 | given and the reasons for the proposal to give that
-- src:7848 | assistance; and
-- src:7850 | (ii) the effect that the giving of the financial assistance
-- src:7851 | would have on the financial position of the company
-- src:7852 | and, where the company is included in a group of
-- src:7853 | corporations consisting of a holding company and a
-- src:7854 | subsidiary or subsidiaries, the effect that the giving
-- src:7855 | of the financial assistance would have on the
-- src:7856 | financial position of the group of corporations,
-- src:7858 | (c) and is accompanied by a copy of a statement made in
-- src:7859 | accordance with a resolution of the directors, setting out
-- src:7860 | the names of any directors who voted against the resolution
-- src:7861 | and the reasons why they so voted, and signed by not less
-- src:7862 | than 2 directors, stating whether, in the opinion of the
-- src:7863 | directors who voted in favour of the resolution, after taking
-- src:7864 | into account the financial position of the company
-- src:7865 | (including future liabilities and contingent liabilities of
-- src:7866 | the company), the giving of the financial assistance would
-- src:7867 | be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the
-- src:7868 | creditors or members of the company or any class of
-- src:7869 | those creditors or members;
@ref s 76(10)(c) (src:7842-7869)
GIVEN `the notice specifying the intention to propose the special resolution sets out particulars of the financial assistance proposed to be given and the reasons for the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice sets out the effect that the giving of the financial assistance would have on the financial position of the company and, where the company is in a group of corporations, of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by a copy of a statement made in accordance with a resolution of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement sets out the names of any directors who voted against the resolution and the reasons why they so voted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors who signed the statement` IS A NUMBER
      `the statement states whether, in the opinion of the directors who voted in favour of the resolution, the giving of the financial assistance would be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the creditors or members of the company or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(c) the notice and the statement are as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice specifying the intention to propose the special resolution sets out particulars of the financial assistance proposed to be given and the reasons for the proposal`
      AND `the notice sets out the effect that the giving of the financial assistance would have on the financial position of the company and, where the company is in a group of corporations, of the group`
      AND `the notice is accompanied by a copy of a statement made in accordance with a resolution of the directors`
      AND `the statement sets out the names of any directors who voted against the resolution and the reasons why they so voted`
      AND `the number of directors who signed the statement` AT LEAST 2
      AND `the statement states whether, in the opinion of the directors who voted in favour of the resolution, the giving of the financial assistance would be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the creditors or members of the company or any class of them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (c) the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution referred to in paragraph (a) as a special resolution sets out ... and is accompanied by a copy of a statement ... signed by not less than 2 directors" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(d): the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution in (b) as a special resolution is accompanied by a copy of the notice, and a copy of the statement, mentioned in (c).
-- src:7871 | (d) the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution
-- src:7872 | referred to in paragraph (b) as a special resolution is
-- src:7873 | accompanied by a copy of the notice, and a copy of the
-- src:7874 | statement, mentioned in paragraph (c);
@ref s 76(10)(d) (src:7871-7874)
GIVEN `paragraph (b) applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution referred to in paragraph (b) is accompanied by a copy of the notice and a copy of the statement mentioned in paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(d) the notice to the parent is accompanied by the notice and statement` MEANS
    IF NOT `paragraph (b) applies to the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "the resolution referred to in paragraph (b)", which exists only where (b) applies
    ELSE (IF `the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution referred to in paragraph (b) is accompanied by a copy of the notice and a copy of the statement mentioned in paragraph (c)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (d) the notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution referred to in paragraph (b) as a special resolution is accompanied by a copy of the notice, and a copy of the statement, mentioned in paragraph (c)" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(e): not later than the day next following the day when the notice in (c) is despatched to members, there is lodged with the Registrar a copy of that notice and a copy of the statement.
-- src:7879 | (e) not later than the day next following the day when the
-- src:7880 | notice mentioned in paragraph (c) is despatched to
-- src:7881 | members of the company there is lodged with the
-- src:7882 | Registrar a copy of that notice and a copy of the
-- src:7883 | statement that accompanied that notice;
@ref s 76(10)(e) (src:7879-7883)
GIVEN `the day the notice was despatched to members of the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the copies were lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the notice was lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the statement that accompanied the notice was lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(e) the copies have been lodged with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF    `a copy of the notice was lodged with the Registrar`
      AND `a copy of the statement that accompanied the notice was lodged with the Registrar`
      AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the notice was despatched to members of the company` `the day the copies were lodged with the Registrar` 1 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (e) not later than the day next following the day when the notice mentioned in paragraph (c) is despatched to members of the company there is lodged with the Registrar a copy of that notice and a copy of the statement" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet; a period the text fixes (item (a)); early lodging is not excluded (fork F-A8)

-- (10)(f): the notice in (c) and a copy of the statement are sent to (i) all members of the company; (ii) all trustees for debenture holders of the company; and (iii) if there are no trustees for,
-- or for a particular class of, debenture holders - all debenture holders, or all debenture holders of that class, whose names are, at the time the notice is despatched, known to the company.
-- src:7885 | (f) the notice mentioned in paragraph (c) and a copy of the
-- src:7886 | statement mentioned in that paragraph are sent to —
-- src:7888 | (i) all members of the company;
-- src:7890 | (ii) all trustees for debenture holders of the company;
-- src:7891 | and
-- src:7893 | (iii) if there are no trustees for, or for a particular class of,
-- src:7894 | debenture holders of the company — all debenture
-- src:7895 | holders, or all debenture holders of that class (as the
-- src:7896 | case may be) of the company whose names are, at the
-- src:7897 | time when the notice is despatched, known to the
-- src:7898 | company;
@ref s 76(10)(f) (src:7885-7898)
GIVEN `the notice and the statement were sent to all members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice and the statement were sent to all trustees for debenture holders of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are debenture holders, or debenture holders of a class, of the company for whom there is no trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice and the statement were sent to all such debenture holders whose names were known to the company when the notice was despatched` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(f) the notice and the statement have been sent to the members and debenture holders` MEANS
    IF    `the notice and the statement were sent to all members of the company`
      AND `the notice and the statement were sent to all trustees for debenture holders of the company`
      AND ((NOT `there are debenture holders, or debenture holders of a class, of the company for whom there is no trustee`) OR `the notice and the statement were sent to all such debenture holders whose names were known to the company when the notice was despatched`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (f) the notice mentioned in paragraph (c) and a copy of the statement mentioned in that paragraph are sent to (i) all members of the company; (ii) all trustees for debenture holders of the company; and (iii) if there are no trustees ... all debenture holders" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(g): the notice in (d) and the accompanying documents are sent to (i) all members of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company; (ii) all trustees for its debenture holders; and (iii) if there are
-- no trustees for, or for a particular class of, its debenture holders - all debenture holders, or all of that class, whose names are known to it when the notice is despatched.
-- src:7900 | (g) the notice mentioned in paragraph (d) and the
-- src:7901 | accompanying documents are sent to —
-- src:7903 | (i) all members of the listed corporation or of the
-- src:7904 | ultimate holding company;
-- src:7906 | (ii) all trustees for debenture holders of the listed
-- src:7907 | corporation or of the ultimate holding company; and
-- src:7909 | (iii) if there are no trustees for, or for a particular class of,
-- src:7910 | debenture holders of the listed corporation or of the
-- src:7911 | ultimate holding company — all debenture holders
-- src:7912 | or debenture holders of that class (as the case may
-- src:7913 | be) of the listed corporation or of the ultimate
-- src:7914 | holding company whose names are, at the time when
-- src:7915 | the notice is despatched, known to the listed
-- src:7916 | corporation or the ultimate holding company;
@ref s 76(10)(g) (src:7900-7916)
GIVEN `paragraph (b) applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice and the accompanying documents were sent to all members of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice and the accompanying documents were sent to all trustees for debenture holders of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are debenture holders, or debenture holders of a class, of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company for whom there is no trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice and the accompanying documents were sent to all such debenture holders whose names were known to the listed corporation or ultimate holding company when the notice was despatched` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(g) the notice and the documents have been sent to the members and debenture holders of the parent` MEANS
    IF NOT `paragraph (b) applies to the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "the listed corporation or of the ultimate holding company", which exist for this purpose only where (b) applies
    ELSE (IF    `the notice and the accompanying documents were sent to all members of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company`
            AND `the notice and the accompanying documents were sent to all trustees for debenture holders of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company`
            AND ((NOT `there are debenture holders, or debenture holders of a class, of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company for whom there is no trustee`) OR `the notice and the accompanying documents were sent to all such debenture holders whose names were known to the listed corporation or ultimate holding company when the notice was despatched`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (g) the notice mentioned in paragraph (d) and the accompanying documents are sent to (i) all members of the listed corporation or of the ultimate holding company; (ii) ...; and (iii) ..." -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(h): within 21 days after the date on which the resolution in (a) is passed or, in a case to which (b) applies, the date on which the resolution referred to in (b) is passed,
-- whichever is the later, a notice (i) setting out the terms of the resolution in (a); and (ii) stating that any of the persons referred to in subsection (12) may, within the period mentioned there,
-- make an application to the Court opposing the giving of the assistance, is published in a daily newspaper circulating generally in Singapore.
-- src:7918 | (h) within 21 days after the date on which the resolution
-- src:7919 | mentioned in paragraph (a) is passed or, in a case to which
-- src:7920 | paragraph (b) applies, the date on which the resolution
-- src:7925 | referred to in that paragraph is passed, whichever is the
-- src:7926 | later, a notice —
-- src:7928 | (i) setting out the terms of the resolution mentioned in
-- src:7929 | paragraph (a); and
-- src:7931 | (ii) stating that any of the persons referred to in
-- src:7932 | subsection (12) may, within the period mentioned
-- src:7933 | in that subsection, make an application to the Court
-- src:7934 | opposing the giving of the financial assistance,
-- src:7936 | (h) is published in a daily newspaper circulating generally in
-- src:7937 | Singapore;
@ref s 76(10)(h) (src:7918-7937)
GIVEN `the day the company passed the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A DATE
      `paragraph (b) applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the listed corporation or ultimate holding company passed the resolution referred to in paragraph (b)` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was published` IS A DATE
      `the notice sets out the terms of the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that any of the persons referred to in subsection (12) may, within the period mentioned in that subsection, make an application to the Court opposing the giving of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is published in a daily newspaper circulating generally in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(h) the notice has been published in time` MEANS
    IF    `the notice sets out the terms of the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)`
      AND `the notice states that any of the persons referred to in subsection (12) may, within the period mentioned in that subsection, make an application to the Court opposing the giving of the financial assistance`
      AND `the notice is published in a daily newspaper circulating generally in Singapore`
      AND `period: the date is within a period after`
            (IF (`paragraph (b) applies to the company` AND `the day the listed corporation or ultimate holding company passed the resolution referred to in paragraph (b)` GREATER THAN `the day the company passed the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)`) THEN `the day the listed corporation or ultimate holding company passed the resolution referred to in paragraph (b)` ELSE `the day the company passed the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)`)
            `the day the notice was published` 21 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (h) within 21 days after the date on which the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a) is passed or, in a case to which paragraph (b) applies, the date on which the resolution referred to in that paragraph is passed, whichever is the later, a notice ... is published in a daily newspaper circulating generally in Singapore" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet; a period the text fixes (item (a)); the later of the two dates starts the period (fork F-A14)

-- (10)(i): no application opposing the giving of the assistance is made within the period mentioned in (12) or, if one or more applications have been made, each has been withdrawn or the Court has
-- approved the giving of the assistance.
-- src:7939 | (i) no application opposing the giving of the financial
-- src:7940 | assistance is made within the period mentioned in
-- src:7941 | subsection (12) or, if such an application or applications
-- src:7942 | has or have been made, the application or each of the
-- src:7943 | applications has been withdrawn or the Court has approved
-- src:7944 | the giving of the financial assistance; and
@ref s 76(10)(i) (src:7939-7944)
GIVEN `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance was made within the period mentioned in subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each such application has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has approved the giving of the financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(i) no application stands in the way of the giving of the assistance` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance was made within the period mentioned in subsection (12)`)
       OR `each such application has been withdrawn`
       OR `the Court has approved the giving of the financial assistance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (i) no application opposing the giving of the financial assistance is made within the period mentioned in subsection (12) or, if such an application or applications has or have been made, the application or each of the applications has been withdrawn or the Court has approved the giving of the financial assistance" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10)(j): the financial assistance is given in accordance with the terms of the resolution in (a) and not earlier than (i) in a case to which (ii) does not apply, the expiration of the period mentioned in (12);
-- or (ii) if applications have been made to the Court within that period, (A) where each has been withdrawn, the withdrawal of the application or of the last of them; or (B) in any other case, the decision of the Court.
-- "Not earlier than the expiration of the period": the assistance may be given from the day after the last day of the period (fork F-A12).
-- src:7946 | (j) the financial assistance is given in accordance with the
-- src:7947 | terms of the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a) and not
-- src:7948 | earlier than —
-- src:7950 | (i) in a case to which sub‑paragraph (ii) does not
-- src:7951 | apply — the expiration of the period mentioned in
-- src:7952 | subsection (12); or
-- src:7954 | (ii) if an application or applications has or have been
-- src:7955 | made to the Court within that period —
-- src:7957 | (A) where the application or each of the
-- src:7958 | applications has been withdrawn — the
-- src:7959 | withdrawal of the application or of the last of
-- src:7960 | the applications to be withdrawn; or
-- src:7962 | (B) in any other case — the decision of the Court
-- src:7963 | on the application or applications.
@ref s 76(10)(j) (src:7946-7963)
GIVEN `the financial assistance is given in accordance with the terms of the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the financial assistance is given` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was published` IS A DATE
      `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance was made within the period mentioned in subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each such application has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the withdrawal of the application or of the last of the applications to be withdrawn` IS A DATE
      `the day of the decision of the Court on the application or applications` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10)(j) the assistance is given in accordance with the resolution and not too early` MEANS
    IF `the financial assistance is given in accordance with the terms of the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)`
    THEN (IF NOT `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance was made within the period mentioned in subsection (12)`
          THEN (IF `the day the financial assistance is given` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice was published` 21 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(j) the financial assistance is given ... not earlier than (i) ... the expiration of the period mentioned in subsection (12)" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet
          ELSE (IF `each such application has been withdrawn`
                THEN (IF `the day the financial assistance is given` AT LEAST `the day of the withdrawal of the application or of the last of the applications to be withdrawn`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(A) where the application or each of the applications has been withdrawn - the withdrawal of the application or of the last of the applications to be withdrawn" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet
                ELSE (IF `the day the financial assistance is given` AT LEAST `the day of the decision of the Court on the application or applications`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(B) in any other case - the decision of the Court on the application or applications" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (j) the financial assistance is given in accordance with the terms of the resolution mentioned in paragraph (a)" -- a condition introduced by "if", unmet

-- (10) as a whole: nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving of financial assistance if (a) to (j). The answers for (b), (d) and (g) may be NOTHING where (b) does not apply: that counts as met.
-- src:7816 | (10) Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company of
-- src:7817 | financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, an
-- src:7818 | acquisition or proposed acquisition by a person of shares or units of
-- src:7819 | shares in the company or in a holding company or ultimate holding
-- src:7820 | company (as the case may be) of the company if —
@ref s 76(10) (src:7816-7820)
GIVEN `the answer for paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (f)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (g)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (h)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for paragraph (j)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` MEANS
    IF    `the answer for paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (`the answer for paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer for paragraph (b)` EQUALS NOTHING)
      AND `the answer for paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (`the answer for paragraph (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer for paragraph (d)` EQUALS NOTHING)
      AND `the answer for paragraph (e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the answer for paragraph (f)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (`the answer for paragraph (g)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer for paragraph (g)` EQUALS NOTHING)
      AND `the answer for paragraph (h)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the answer for paragraph (i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the answer for paragraph (j)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in subsection (1) prohibits the giving by a company of financial assistance ... if (a) ... (j)" -- a carve-out named for a permission whose "if" gate failed {F-A7}

§ `Section 76(10A): resolutions passed by written means`

-- (10A): if the resolution in (10)(a) or (b) is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A, (10)(f) or (g) (as the case may be) must be complied with at or before the time
-- (a) agreement to the resolution is sought in accordance with section 184C; or (b) the documents referred to in section 183(3A) are served on or made accessible to members, as the case may be.
-- The text says "time"; the function compares days (fork F-A15).
-- src:7967 | (10A) If the resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(a) or (b) is
-- src:7968 | proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A,
-- src:7973 | subsection (10)(f) or (g) (as the case may be) must be complied with
-- src:7974 | at or before the time —
-- src:7976 | (a) agreement to the resolution is sought in accordance with
-- src:7977 | section 184C; or
-- src:7979 | (b) documents referred to in section 183(3A) in respect of the
-- src:7980 | resolution are served on or made accessible to members of
-- src:7981 | the company in accordance with section 183(3A),
-- src:7983 | as the case may be.
@ref s 76(10A) (src:7967-7983)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice and the statement or documents were sent as paragraph (f) or (g) requires` IS A DATE
      `the day agreement to the resolution is sought under section 184C, or the documents are served on or made accessible to members under section 183(3A), as the case may be` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(10A) paragraph (f) or (g) has been complied with in time for a resolution by written means` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the resolution ... is proposed to be passed by written means under section 184A" -- the subsection speaks of that case only
    ELSE (IF `the day the notice and the statement or documents were sent as paragraph (f) or (g) requires` AT MOST `the day agreement to the resolution is sought under section 184C, or the documents are served on or made accessible to members under section 183(3A), as the case may be`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (10)(f) or (g) (as the case may be) must be complied with at or before the time" -- the duty not met in time

§ `Section 76(11): the Court's declaration of compliance`

-- (11): where, on application to the Court by a company, the Court is satisfied that the provisions of (10) have been substantially complied with in relation to a proposed giving of financial assistance,
-- the Court may, by order, declare that they have been complied with.
-- src:7985 | (11) Where, on application to the Court by a company, the Court is
-- src:7986 | satisfied that the provisions of subsection (10) have been
-- src:7987 | substantially complied with in relation to a proposed giving by the
-- src:7988 | company of financial assistance of a kind mentioned in that
-- src:7989 | subsection, the Court may, by order, declare that the provisions of
-- src:7990 | that subsection have been complied with in relation to the proposed
-- src:7991 | giving by the company of financial assistance.
@ref s 76(11) (src:7985-7991)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the provisions of subsection (10) have been substantially complied with in relation to the proposed giving of financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(11) the Court may declare that the provisions of subsection (10) have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied to the Court` AND `the Court is satisfied that the provisions of subsection (10) have been substantially complied with in relation to the proposed giving of financial assistance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on application to the Court by a company, the Court is satisfied that the provisions of subsection (10) have been substantially complied with ... the Court may, by order, declare" -- a "may" function gated by "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); listed in group G1 (fork F-A6), the other reading is NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12)

§ `Section 76(12): who may oppose`

-- (12): where a special resolution mentioned in (10)(a) is passed, an application to the Court opposing the giving of the assistance may be made, within the period of 21 days after the publication of the
-- notice mentioned in (10)(h), (a) by a member of the company; (b) by a trustee for debenture holders; (c) by a debenture holder; (d) by a creditor; (e) if (10)(b) applies, by (i) a member of the listed
-- corporation or ultimate holding company that passed the special resolution, (ii) its trustee for debenture holders, (iii) its debenture holder, or (iv) its creditor; or (f) by the Registrar.
-- src:7993 | (12) Where a special resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(a) is
-- src:7994 | passed by a company, an application to the Court opposing the giving
-- src:7995 | of the financial assistance to which the special resolution relates may
-- src:7996 | be made, within the period of 21 days after the publication of the
-- src:7997 | notice mentioned in subsection (10)(h) —
-- src:7999 | (a) by a member of the company;
-- src:8001 | (b) by a trustee for debenture holders of the company;
-- src:8003 | (c) by a debenture holder of the company;
-- src:8005 | (d) by a creditor of the company;
-- src:8007 | (e) if subsection (10)(b) applies by —
-- src:8009 | (i) a member of the listed corporation or ultimate
-- src:8010 | holding company that passed a special resolution
-- src:8011 | mentioned in that subsection;
-- src:8013 | (ii) a trustee for debenture holders of that listed
-- src:8014 | corporation or ultimate holding company;
-- src:8016 | (iii) a debenture holder of that listed corporation or
-- src:8017 | ultimate holding company; or
-- src:8022 | (iv) a creditor of that listed corporation or ultimate
-- src:8023 | holding company; or
-- src:8025 | (f) by the Registrar.
@ref s 76(12) (src:7993-8025)
GIVEN `a special resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(a) has been passed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice mentioned in subsection (10)(h) was published` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      applicant IS A `s 76(12) applicant`
      `paragraph (b) applies to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(12) the person may apply to the Court opposing the giving of the assistance` MEANS
    IF NOT `a special resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(a) has been passed by the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a special resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(a) is passed by a company, an application ... may be made" -- a "may" function gated by "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); listed in group G1 (fork F-A6), the other reading is NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12)
    ELSE (IF NOT (`period: the date is within a period after` `the day the notice mentioned in subsection (10)(h) was published` `the day the application is made` 21 Days)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made, within the period of 21 days after the publication of the notice" -- outside a period the text fixes: periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)
          ELSE CONSIDER applicant
               WHEN `s 76(12)(a) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 76(12)(b) a trustee for debenture holders of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 76(12)(c) a debenture holder of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 76(12)(d) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 76(12)(f) the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 76(12)(e)(i) a member of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company that passed a special resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(b)` THEN (IF `paragraph (b) applies to the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if subsection (10)(b) applies by" -- a grant named for the applicant whose "if" gate failed {F-A7}
               WHEN `s 76(12)(e)(ii) a trustee for debenture holders of that listed corporation or ultimate holding company` THEN (IF `paragraph (b) applies to the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if subsection (10)(b) applies by" {F-A7}
               WHEN `s 76(12)(e)(iii) a debenture holder of that listed corporation or ultimate holding company` THEN (IF `paragraph (b) applies to the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if subsection (10)(b) applies by" {F-A7}
               WHEN `s 76(12)(e)(iv) a creditor of that listed corporation or ultimate holding company` THEN (IF `paragraph (b) applies to the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if subsection (10)(b) applies by" {F-A7}
               OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list (a) to (f) is not closed with "only", and the subsection says nothing of any other person

§ `Section 76(13): what the Court must do and may do on an opposing application`

-- (13)(a): where an application or applications opposing the giving of financial assistance under a special resolution are made under (12), the Court must, in determining what order or orders to
-- make, have regard to the rights and interests of the members of the company or any class of them as well as of the creditors of the company or any class of them.
-- src:8027 | (13) Where an application or applications opposing the giving of
-- src:8028 | financial assistance by a company in accordance with a special
-- src:8029 | resolution passed by the company is or are made to the Court under
-- src:8030 | subsection (12), the Court —
-- src:8032 | (a) must, in determining what order or orders to make in
-- src:8033 | relation to the application or applications, have regard to
-- src:8034 | the rights and interests of the members of the company or
-- src:8035 | of any class of them as well as to the rights and interests of
-- src:8036 | the creditors of the company or of any class of them; and
@ref s 76(13)(a) (src:8027-8036)
GIVEN `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance has been made to the Court under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(13)(a) the Court must have regard to the rights and interests of the members and of the creditors` MEANS
    IF `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance has been made to the Court under subsection (12)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application or applications opposing the giving of financial assistance ... is or are made to the Court under subsection (12), the Court (a) must ... have regard" -- a "where" gate that fails: periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b) (fork F-A6, group G1)

-- (13)(b): the Court must not make an order approving the giving of the assistance unless it is satisfied that (i) the company has disclosed to the members all material matters relating to the proposed
-- assistance; and (ii) the proposed assistance would not, after taking into account the financial position of the company (including any future or contingent liabilities), be likely to prejudice materially
-- the interests of the creditors or members of the company or of any class of them.
-- src:8038 | (b) must not make an order approving the giving of the
-- src:8039 | financial assistance unless the Court is satisfied that —
-- src:8041 | (i) the company has disclosed to the members of the
-- src:8042 | company all material matters relating to the proposed
-- src:8043 | financial assistance; and
-- src:8045 | (ii) the proposed financial assistance would not, after
-- src:8046 | taking into account the financial position of the
-- src:8047 | company (including any future or contingent
-- src:8048 | liabilities), be likely to prejudice materially the
-- src:8049 | interests of the creditors or members of the
-- src:8050 | company or of any class of those creditors or
-- src:8051 | members,
@ref s 76(13)(b) (src:8038-8051)
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied that the company has disclosed to the members of the company all material matters relating to the proposed financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the proposed financial assistance would not, after taking into account the financial position of the company (including any future or contingent liabilities), be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the creditors or members of the company or of any class of those creditors or members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(13)(b) the Court is barred from making an order approving the giving of the assistance` MEANS
    IF    `the Court is satisfied that the company has disclosed to the members of the company all material matters relating to the proposed financial assistance`
      AND `the Court is satisfied that the proposed financial assistance would not, after taking into account the financial position of the company (including any future or contingent liabilities), be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the creditors or members of the company or of any class of those creditors or members`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not make an order approving the giving of the financial assistance unless the Court is satisfied that (i) ... and (ii) ..." -- the bar is lifted by its own "unless"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (13)(b), the orders: the Court "may do all or any of the following": (iii) if it thinks fit, make an order for the purchase by the company of the interests of dissentient members and the reduction
-- accordingly of its capital; (iv) if it thinks fit, adjourn the proceedings so that an arrangement may be made for the purchase of those interests otherwise than by the company or a subsidiary;
-- (v) give ancillary or consequential directions and make ancillary or consequential orders as it thinks expedient; (vi) make an order disapproving the giving or, subject to paragraph (b), approving it.
-- (In the rendering the closing words stand under a repeated label "(b)": NOTES.md, finding.)
-- src:8053 | (b) and may do all or any of the following:
-- src:8055 | (iii) if it thinks fit, make an order for the purchase by the
-- src:8056 | company of the interests of dissentient members of
-- src:8057 | the company and for the reduction accordingly of the
-- src:8058 | capital of the company;
-- src:8060 | (iv) if it thinks fit, adjourn the proceedings in order that
-- src:8061 | an arrangement may be made to the satisfaction of
-- src:8062 | the Court for the purchase (otherwise than by the
-- src:8063 | company or by a subsidiary of the company) of the
-- src:8064 | interests of dissentient members;
-- src:8069 | (v) give such ancillary or consequential directions and
-- src:8070 | make such ancillary or consequential orders as it
-- src:8071 | thinks expedient;
-- src:8073 | (vi) make an order disapproving the giving of the
-- src:8074 | financial assistance or, subject to paragraph (b), an
-- src:8075 | order approving the giving of the financial
-- src:8076 | assistance.
@ref s 76(13)(b) (src:8053-8076)
GIVEN `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance has been made to the Court under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order` IS A `s 76(13) order of the Court`
      `the Court is satisfied that the company has disclosed to the members of the company all material matters relating to the proposed financial assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the proposed financial assistance would not, after taking into account the financial position of the company (including any future or contingent liabilities), be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the creditors or members of the company or of any class of those creditors or members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(13) the Court may make the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application opposing the giving of the financial assistance has been made to the Court under subsection (12)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application or applications opposing the giving ... is or are made to the Court under subsection (12), the Court ... may do all or any of the following" -- a "may" function gated by "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); listed in group G1 (fork F-A6), the other reading is NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the order`
         WHEN `s 76(13)(b)(iii) an order for the purchase by the company of the interests of dissentient members and the reduction accordingly of the capital of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76(13)(b)(iv) an adjournment of the proceedings so that an arrangement may be made for the purchase, otherwise than by the company or a subsidiary of it, of the interests of dissentient members` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76(13)(b)(v) ancillary or consequential directions or orders` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76(13)(b)(vi) an order disapproving the giving of the financial assistance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 76(13)(b)(vi) an order approving the giving of the financial assistance` THEN (IF `s 76(13)(b) the Court is barred from making an order approving the giving of the assistance` `the Court is satisfied that the company has disclosed to the members of the company all material matters relating to the proposed financial assistance` `the Court is satisfied that the proposed financial assistance would not, after taking into account the financial position of the company (including any future or contingent liabilities), be likely to prejudice materially the interests of the creditors or members of the company or of any class of those creditors or members` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to paragraph (b), an order approving the giving of the financial assistance" and "must not make an order approving ... unless"
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may do all or any of the following" -- the list is not closed with "only" and the paragraph says nothing of any other order

§ `Section 76(14): lodging the Court's order`

-- (14): where the Court makes an order under this section in relation to the giving of financial assistance by a company, the company must, within 14 days after the order is made, lodge with the Registrar a copy of the order.
-- src:8078 | (14) Where the Court makes an order under this section in relation
-- src:8079 | to the giving of financial assistance by a company, the company must,
-- src:8080 | within 14 days after the order is made, lodge with the Registrar a copy
-- src:8081 | of the order.
@ref s 76(14) (src:8078-8081)
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the company lodged a copy of the order with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the company lodged a copy of the order with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(14) the company has lodged a copy of the order with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF `the company lodged a copy of the order with the Registrar` AND `period: the date is within a period after` `the day the order was made` `the day the company lodged a copy of the order with the Registrar` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, within 14 days after the order is made, lodge with the Registrar a copy of the order" -- a duty not met in a period the text fixes (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- The same duty as a rule: the company MUST lodge a copy of the order WITHIN 14 days; missing the deadline is BREACH. The clock counts days from the order (day 0).
-- src:8078 | (14) Where the Court makes an order under this section in relation
-- src:8079 | to the giving of financial assistance by a company, the company must,
-- src:8080 | within 14 days after the order is made, lodge with the Registrar a copy
-- src:8081 | of the order.
@ref s 76(14) (src:8078-8081)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76 act`
`s 76(14) the company must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 76(14) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the order of the Court`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar within 14 days after the order was made"

§ `Section 76(15): directors' duties are not relieved by the special resolution or the Court's approval`

-- (15): the passing of a special resolution for the giving of financial assistance, and the approval by the Court of the giving, do not relieve a director of any duty to the company under section 157 or otherwise.
-- src:8083 | (15) The passing of a special resolution by a company for the giving
-- src:8084 | of financial assistance by the company for the purpose of, or in
-- src:8085 | connection with, an acquisition or proposed acquisition of shares or
-- src:8086 | units of shares in the company, and the approval by the Court of the
-- src:8087 | giving of the financial assistance, do not relieve a director of the
-- src:8088 | company of any duty to the company under section 157 or otherwise,
-- src:8089 | and whether of a fiduciary nature or not, in connection with the giving
-- src:8090 | of the financial assistance.
@ref s 76(15) (src:8083-8090)
GIVEN `a special resolution for the giving of the financial assistance has been passed, or the Court has approved the giving` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(15) the director is relieved of the director's duty to the company by the special resolution or the Court's approval` MEANS
    IF `a special resolution for the giving of the financial assistance has been passed, or the Court has approved the giving`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not relieve a director of the company of any duty to the company under section 157 or otherwise, and whether of a fiduciary nature or not" (a flat negative, ruling N2 of 2026-11-04)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of relief by that resolution or approval and says nothing of relief by any other means
